From: Jason Rhinelander <jason@imaginary.ca>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:02:17 -0300
Subject: Add --db-slow-query-ms to log slow database statements

Off by default.  When set, every pooled connection gets an sqlite profile
callback that logs any statement taking at least that long, with its SQL
text (never the bound values, which would put message payloads in the
log).

sqlite times a statement from its first step to its completion or reset,
which includes any time spent in the busy handler, so a slow
BEGIN IMMEDIATE identifies a writer waiting on another rather than slow
work of its own.  This is meant for tracking down the occasional
"database is locked" failures: the holder of the write lock is the slow
statement inside a transaction or the slow autocommit write, not the
one that timed out.
